<title>SPAIN: Spain Q4 earnings up 4.4 pct, '96 earnings up 4.5.</title>
<headline>Spain Q4 earnings up 4.4 pct, '96 earnings up 4.5.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average wages in Spain per worker per month rose 4.4 percent year-on-year in the fourth quarter, and 4.5 percent in 1996 overall, National Statistics Institute INE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In the third quarter earnings rose 4.6 percent.</p>
<p>By sector, in the fourth quarter wages rose 5.3 percent in industry, by 4.5 percent in construction and by 3.3 percent in services.</p>
<p>In 1996 on average, industry wages rose 5.5 percent, construction earnings rose 4.5 percent and services rose 3.3 percent.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
